      "description": "Bonn, Germany: Konrad Adenauer head (first chancellor of the Federal Republic of Germany from 1949 till 1963); memorial in front of the former Federal Chancellery, Bundeskanzlerplatz nearby Adenauer-Allee.\nDescription on separate sign :\nKonrad Adenauer\nborn 1876\ndied 1967\nThe first Federal Chancellor of the Federal Republic of Germany \nfrom 1949 to 1963 who stamped the policy of this time\nthe reconciliation with France initiated \nand prepared for the European arrangement ways.\nThe monument plastic also points to life stations \nof the statesman with modeled pictogrammes and assigned annual figures, \nas for example Cologne Cathedral,\nPrussian eagle, Federal Chancellor, cathedral of Reims, \nSiebengebirge, Europe on the bull.\nsculptor: Hubertus von Pilgrim, Munich\n\ninstallation: may 1982",
